1. Exception Hierarchy Proposal (exceptions.py)

Yes — rejected user actions and stored-file integrity failures should sit on separate branches of WalletError, so ui/ knows immediately whether to halt the app or display a recoverable error and let the user try again without relying on call-site guesswork.
